{"id":"mahabharata-1-209","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":209,"title":"नवाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 209 · The apsarases freed; the birth of Babhruvahana","summary":{"en":"The apsaras Varga relates how Narada told them a great hero would free them; Arjuna frees all five. He returns to Manipura, where Chitrangada has borne him a son, Babhruvahana, and then goes on to Gokarna.","kn":"ಒಬ್ಬ ಮಹಾವೀರನು ತಮ್ಮನ್ನು ಬಿಡಿಸುವನೆಂದು ನಾರದರು ಹೇಳಿದ್ದನ್ನು ಅಪ್ಸರೆ ವರ್ಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಐವರನ್ನೂ ಬಿಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವನು ಮಣಿಪುರಕ್ಕೆ ಮರಳಿದಾಗ ಚಿತ್ರಾಂಗದೆ ಬಭ್ರುವಾಹನನೆಂಬ ಮಗನನ್ನು ಹೆತ್ತಿರುತ್ತಾಳೆ; ಅನಂತರ ಗೋಕರ್ಣಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अप्सरा वर्गा बताती है कि नारद ने कहा था कि एक महान वीर उन्हें मुक्त करेगा; अर्जुन पाँचों को मुक्त करते हैं। वे मणिपुर लौटते हैं, जहाँ चित्राङ्गदा ने बभ्रुवाहन नामक पुत्र को जन्म दिया है, और फिर गोकर्ण जाते हैं।","te":"ఒక మహావీరుడు తమను విడిపిస్తాడని నారదుడు చెప్పిన విషయాన్ని అప్సరస వర్గ వివరిస్తుంది; అర్జునుడు ఐదుగురినీ విడిపిస్తాడు. అతడు మణిపురానికి తిరిగి రాగా చిత్రాంగద బభ్రువాహనుడనే కుమారుని కని ఉంటుంది; తర్వాత గోకర్ణానికి వెళ్తాడు.","ta":"ஒரு பெரும் வீரன் தம்மை விடுவிப்பான் என்று நாரதர் சொன்னதை அப்ஸரஸ் வர்கை சொல்கிறாள்; அர்ஜுனன் ஐவரையும் விடுவிக்கிறான். அவன் மணிபுரம் திரும்பியபோது சித்ராங்கதை பப்ருவாஹனன் என்ற மகனைப் பெற்றிருக்கிறாள்; பின்னர் அவன் கோகர்ணம் செல்கிறான்.","ml":"അപ്സരസ്സായ വർഗ, തങ്ങളെ മോചിപ്പിക്കുന്ന ഒരു മഹാവീരൻ വരുമെന്ന് നാരദൻ അറിയിച്ചതായി പറയുന്നു; അർജുനൻ അഞ്ചു പേരെയും മോചിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. അദ്ദേഹം മണിപ്പുരത്ത് മടങ്ങിയെത്തുന്നു, അവിടെ ചിത്രാംഗദ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് ബഭ്രുവാഹനൻ എന്ന പുത്രനെ പ്രസവിച്ചിരിക്കുന്നു; പിന്നീട് അദ്ദേഹം ഗോകർണത്തിലേക്ക് പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.209; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अर्जुनवनवासपर्व","titleEn":"Arjunavanavasa Parva (Arjuna's forest exile)","verses":[{"text":"वर्गोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Varga said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो वयं प्रव्यथिताः सर्वा भरतसत्तम ।\nआयाम शरणं विप्रं तं तपोधनमच्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all of us, deeply distressed, went to that Brahmin, ascetic and unshaken, to seek his refuge, O best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":2,"text":"रूपेण वयसा चैव कन्दर्पेण च दर्पिताः ।\nअयुक्तं कृतवत्यः स्म क्षन्तुमर्हसि नो द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"We were proud of our beauty, youth and desire, and we acted improperly; you ought to forgive us, twice-born one."}},{"n":3,"text":"एष एव वधोऽस्माकं सुपर्याप्तस्तपोधन ।\nयद्वयं संशितात्मानं प्रलोब्धुं त्वामिहागताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This alone is punishment enough for us, ascetic, that we came here to tempt you, a man of fixed mind."}},{"n":4,"text":"अवध्यास्तु स्त्रियः सृष्टा मन्यन्ते धर्मचिन्तकाः ।\nतस्माद्धर्मेण धर्मज्ञ नास्मान्हिंसितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinkers on dharma hold that women were created as not to be killed; so by dharma, knower of dharma, you should not harm us."}},{"n":5,"text":"सर्वभूतेषु धर्मज्ञ मैत्रो ब्राह्मण उच्यते ।\nसत्यो भवतु कल्याण एष वादो मनीषिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Brahmin is said to be friendly to all beings, knower of dharma; let this saying of the wise be true, good sir."}},{"n":6,"text":"शरणं च प्रपन्नानां शिष्टाः कुर्वन्ति पालनम् ।\nशरणं त्वां प्रपन्नाः स्म तस्मात्त्वं क्षन्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The good protect those who come to them for refuge; we have come to you for refuge, so you should forgive us."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु धर्मात्मा ब्राह्मणः शुभकर्मकृत् ।\nप्रसादं कृतवान्वीर रविसोमसमप्रभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the righteous Brahmin of auspicious deeds, shining like the sun and moon, showed his grace, hero."}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Brahmin said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"शतं सहस्रं विश्वं च सर्वमक्षयवाचकम् ।\nपरिमाणं शतं त्वेतन्नैतदक्षयवाचकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hundred, thousand and all are words for the inexhaustible; but here a hundred is a measure, not a word for the endless."}},{"n":9,"text":"यदा च वो ग्राहभूता गृह्णन्तीः पुरुषाञ्जले ।\nउत्कर्षति जलात्कश्चित्स्थलं पुरुषसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When you, become crocodiles, seize men in the water, and some best of men drags one of you from the water onto land,"}},{"n":10,"text":"तदा यूयं पुनः सर्वाः स्वरूपं प्रतिपत्स्यथ ।\nअनृतं नोक्तपूर्वं मे हसतापि कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"then all of you shall regain your own forms. I have never spoken an untruth, even in jest."}},{"n":11,"text":"तानि सर्वाणि तीर्थानि इतः प्रभृति चैव ह ।\nनारीतीर्थानि नाम्नेह ख्यातिं यास्यन्ति सर्वशः ।\nपुण्यानि च भविष्यन्ति पावनानि मनीषिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From now on all those tirthas shall be famed everywhere by the name Nari-tirthas, and they shall be holy and purifying for the wise."}},{"text":"वर्गोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Varga said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"ततोऽभिवाद्य तं विप्रं कृत्वा चैव प्रदक्षिणम् ।\nअचिन्तयामोपसृत्य तस्माद्देशात्सुदुःखिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then we bowed to that Brahmin, circled him, and left that place, greatly sorrowful, wondering:"}},{"n":13,"text":"क्व नु नाम वयं सर्वाः कालेनाल्पेन तं नरम् ।\nसमागच्छेम यो नस्तद्रूपमापादयेत्पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where, and in how short a time, shall we meet the man who will restore our former forms?"}},{"n":14,"text":"ता वयं चिन्तयित्वैवं मुहूर्तादिव भारत ।\nदृष्टवत्यो महाभागं देवर्षिमुत नारदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As we thought thus, O Bharata, in a moment we saw the great and fortunate divine sage Narada."}},{"n":15,"text":"सर्वा हृष्टाः स्म तं दृष्ट्वा देवर्षिममितद्युतिम् ।\nअभिवाद्य च तं पार्थ स्थिताः स्म व्यथिताननाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We were all glad to see that divine sage of boundless splendor; bowing to him, Partha, we stood with troubled faces."}},{"n":16,"text":"स नोऽपृच्छद्दुःखमूलमुक्तवत्यो वयं च तत् ।\nश्रुत्वा तच्च यथावृत्तमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He asked us the root of our grief, and we told it; having heard it all as it happened, he spoke these words."}},{"n":17,"text":"दक्षिणे सागरानूपे पञ्च तीर्थानि सन्ति वै ।\nपुण्यानि रमणीयानि तानि गच्छत माचिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the southern shore of the sea there are five tirthas, holy and delightful; go there without delay."}},{"n":18,"text":"तत्राशु पुरुषव्याघ्रः पाण्डवो वो धनंजयः ।\nमोक्षयिष्यति शुद्धात्मा दुःखादस्मान्न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the tiger among men, the Pandava Dhananjaya, pure in spirit, will quickly free you from this misery; there is no doubt."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्य सर्वा वयं वीर श्रुत्वा वाक्यमिहागताः ।\nतदिदं सत्यमेवाद्य मोक्षिताहं त्वयानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, hero, all of us came here; and today this is true, for I have been freed by you, sinless one."}},{"n":20,"text":"एतास्तु मम वै सख्यश्चतस्रोऽन्या जले स्थिताः ।\nकुरु कर्म शुभं वीर एताः सर्वा विमोक्षय ॥","meaning":{"en":"These other four friends of mine still stay in the water. Do this good deed, hero, and free them all."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"ततस्ताः पाण्डवश्रेष्ठः सर्वा एव विशां पते ।\nतस्माच्छापाददीनात्मा मोक्षयामास वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the best of the Pandavas, strong and of unbroken spirit, freed all of them, O lord of the people, from that curse."}},{"n":22,"text":"उत्थाय च जलात्तस्मात्प्रतिलभ्य वपुः स्वकम् ।\nतास्तदाप्सरसो राजन्नदृश्यन्त यथा पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rising from the water and regaining their own bodies, those apsarases were seen as before, O king."}},{"n":23,"text":"तीर्थानि शोधयित्वा तु तथानुज्ञाय ताः प्रभुः ।\nचित्राङ्गदां पुनर्द्रष्टुं मणलूरपुरं ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having cleansed the tirthas and given the women leave to go, the lord went again to the city of Manalura to see Chitrangada."}},{"n":24,"text":"तस्यामजनयत्पुत्रं राजानं बभ्रुवाहनम् ।\nतं दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवो राजन्गोकर्णमभितोऽगमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He begot on her a son, King Babhruvahana; and seeing him, the Pandava, O king, went on toward Gokarna."}}]}]}